<title>UK: Virgin to sweeten rail franchise bid --paper.</title>
<headline>Virgin to sweeten rail franchise bid --paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Richard Branson's Virgin Group has underlined its bid to run the West Coast Main Line rail franchise with a pledge to invest 750 million stg in new rolling stock if successful, the Guardian newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Virgin, already committed to spending 250 million stg on new rolling stock for the CrossCountry rail franchise, is talking to bankers, leasing companies and rolling stock manufacturers about how to finance the order, the Guardian said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
